{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011WvtiBUuNCS6NctvqVLM4z","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me analyze the research context carefully to define three tiers for the Dream simulation.\n\nKey facts from the context:\n1. The project has two contributions: episode-level training methodology + selective verification\n2. Claim 1 (episode-level credit assignment) is marked as \"ESTABLISHED\" based on exp029 step5 val=25% vs exp028c step10 val=0%\n3. BUT plan_001 (exp029 continuation) has conclusion: \"failed\" and exp029_episode_level in registry also shows \"failed\"\n4. The target is ≥40% success rate for the episode-level training to support the cost-efficiency story\n\n\n5. Phase B (selective verification) hasn't started yet, and there's a contingency plan if success falls short of 40%\n\nLooking at the experiment history, I'm seeing a pattern of early promise followed by convergence failures—exp029 hit 25% at step 5 but ultimately didn't reach the 40% threshold, while exp028c collapsed entirely by step 10. The best sustained success rates across all attempts have been in the 20-35% range, which raises questions about whether episode-level training alone can achieve the necessary performance, whether selective verification will succeed, and whether the episode-level insight is sufficiently novel if the primary contribution underperforms.\n\nNow I'm mapping out three scenarios based on where the training converges. The best case would be episode-level success reaching 45-60%, enabling selective verification to deliver the full dual-contribution story with strong cost-efficiency gains. The median case sits at 30-45% convergence—borderline enough to attempt selective verification but requiring a heavier emphasis on the training methodology itself. The worst case plateaus below 30%, forcing a reframe toward a pure training methodology paper without the verification component.\n\nI'm also thinking through the ablation metrics: the h-sweep should ideally show a clear monotonic degradation pattern that confirms the gamma mechanism, though noisier results would still support the general trend. For selective verification specifically, I'm looking at whether we can achieve 40%+ reduction in verification costs with minimal success rate degradation, versus more modest improvements that weaken the efficiency narrative.\n\nWriting the YAML output...","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":16677,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":16677},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"35399d2b-f3c5-4a3e-b0c1-7f219f514605","uuid":"423e85d1-bf56-4ea4-b1cc-a8de3a5927d8"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011WvtiBUuNCS6NctvqVLM4z","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```yaml\ntiers:\n  best:\n    meaning: \"Episode-level训练收敛至≥45%，selective verification完整验证，dual contribution成立\"\n    key_assumptions:\n      - \"Episode-level GRPO在continued training中突破40%阈值并稳定收敛\"\n      - \"h-sweep展示清晰的单调退化+sharp cliff，机制分析compelling\"\n      - \"Action-change作为intrinsic reward有效训练selective policy\"\n      - \"B-IAVR在verification↓40%+的同时success delta<3pp\"\n      - \"Multi-seed复现std<5pp\"\n    number_ranges:\n      episode_level_success_rate: [45, 60]\n      step_independent_baseline: [0, 6]\n      h_sweep_cliff_threshold: [5, 10]\n      selective_verification_rate_reduction: [40, 60]\n      selective_vs_always_on_success_delta_pp: [0, 3]\n      action_change_confirmatory_rate_pct: [60, 80]\n      multi_seed_std_pp: [1, 5]\n      action_is_valid: [90, 98]\n    narrative_direction: \"原始dual-contribution framing完全成立。Story: step-independent RL在multi-turn agent上灾难性失败→episode-level解决credit assignment→在此基础上action-change reward训练selective verification→near-always-on performance at 40-60% lower cost。两个contribution互相支撑，Claim 1是enabling methodology，Claim 2+3是downstream application。\"\n\n  median:\n    meaning: \"Episode-level收敛至30-42%，selective verification效果有限，需rebalance为methodology-heavy paper\"\n    key_assumptions:\n      - \"Episode-level训练收敛但未大幅超过40%阈值（borderline区间）\"\n      - \"h-sweep大体展示预期趋势但存在噪声（某些h值不完全单调）\"\n      - \"Selective verification可训练但cost-performance tradeoff不dramatic\"\n      - \"Action-change signal存在但correlation moderate（r=0.15-0.25）\"\n      - \"Multi-seed有一定variance（std 5-8pp）\"\n    number_ranges:\n      episode_level_success_rate: [30, 42]\n      step_independent_baseline: [0, 6]\n      h_sweep_cliff_threshold: [3, 8]\n      selective_verification_rate_reduction: [15, 35]\n      selective_vs_always_on_success_delta_pp: [3, 8]\n      action_change_confirmatory_rate_pct: [55, 75]\n      multi_seed_std_pp: [5, 8]\n      action_is_valid: [85, 93]\n    narrative_direction: \"Rebalance为70% training methodology + 30% selective verification。Claim 1保持strong（episode vs step-independent的gap仍然dramatic），但Claim 2+3降级为'preliminary evidence'或'proof-of-concept'。Paper主打：episode-level training是被忽视的关键设计选择，selective verification作为downstream application demo而非co-equal contribution。需要加厚Phase C ablation（h-sweep做得更细、mechanism analysis更深）来补偿Phase B的弱结果。Title可能调整为更强调methodology。\"\n\n  worst:\n    meaning: \"Episode-level收敛停滞在20-30%，selective verification无法有意义地执行，需完全reframe为pure methodology paper\"\n    key_assumptions:\n      - \"Episode-level训练plateau在20-30%（高于baseline但远不够支撑cost story）\"\n      - \"Success rate不足以让selective verification有统计意义上的对比空间\"\n      - \"h-sweep仍能展示episode-level vs step-independent的gap，但绝对性能不impressive\"\n      - \"Multi-seed variance较大（std>8pp），削弱统计credibility\"\n      - \"1.7B model可能是性能瓶颈而非方法问题（reviewer会attack）\"\n    number_ranges:\n      episode_level_success_rate: [20, 30]\n      step_independent_baseline: [0, 6]\n      h_sweep_cliff_threshold: [2, 6]\n      selective_verification_rate_reduction: [0, 15]\n      selective_vs_always_on_success_delta_pp: [8, 15]\n      action_change_confirmatory_rate_pct: [50, 70]\n      multi_seed_std_pp: [8, 12]\n      action_is_valid: [80, 90]\n    narrative_direction: \"完全放弃selective verification contribution，执行Contingency Plan A：pure training methodology paper 'Episode-Level RL for Multi-Turn Agents: Why Step-Independent Fails and How to Fix It'。Core argument转为：(1)揭示现有LLM-agent RL工作（RAGEN等）的隐性failure mode，(2)提供mechanistic explanation（gamma^(T-h) decay），(3)提出fix并在multiple h values上验证。需要大量invest在：h-sweep做极细粒度（h=1,2,3,5,8,10,15,20,full）、mechanism visualization（Figure 2成为paper核心）、与RAGEN/existing work的explicit对比展示他们默认step-independent。可能需要ScienceWorld第二环境来弥补single-env weakness。不降venue——methodology insight本身sufficiently novel for top venue，但需要更深的analysis depth。\"\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":16677,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":16677},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"35399d2b-f3c5-4a3e-b0c1-7f219f514605","uuid":"91b87d8b-cfca-4b31-ae78-b20b05c93183"}
